  // ─── [POST-AUDIT] ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The coverage audit reads a SIMULATION — the document as it WOULD read
  // if every edit applied. When an edit then fails to anchor, that
  // simulation was fiction and the verdict described a document that does
  // not exist.
  //
  // Seen on a three-way NDA conversion: the mediation clause and the
  // assignment carve-out were both planned, both dropped by a failed
  // anchor, and the pre-apply audit still read "covered" because the
  // simulation had them. Asking afterwards found both immediately.
  //
  // So re-read the real paragraphs and score the SAME checklist against
  // what is actually on the page.
  // TO REMOVE: delete to [/POST-AUDIT] + its call at the end of _runChain
